                    {
                        "sense_id": "b43f4b03-09a2-36a8-83c2-cdbd4738b692",
                        "entry_id": "5c2d6ac5-ccc7-3264-a247-1cd6c49ec4ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Modus des Verbs, der die Befehlsform an die 3. Person ausdrückt und im Deutschen mit dem Konjunktiv I gebildet wird (imperativisch gebrauchter Konjunktiv)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fc2e084-b73f-407d-8e25-e0d2bff92013",
                                "sense_id": "b43f4b03-09a2-36a8-83c2-cdbd4738b692",
                                "text": "Im Kashmiri ist der Jussiv flexionsmorphologisch kodiert."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "89bc6b79-3380-4a84-93ae-b7c0433a5b2d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c2d6ac5-ccc7-3264-a247-1cd6c49ec4ed",
                        "source_sense_id": "b43f4b03-09a2-36a8-83c2-cdbd4738b692",
                        "target_lang_word": "jussive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jussive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8f64782-0ea9-3749-a3e6-b7032e69ae64",
                                        "entry_id": "5ff18e31-b6c8-31b6-96ba-2fb37d7d11b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The jussive mood, a verb inflection used to indicate a command, permission or agreement with a request; an instance of a verb so inflected."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fe1c471-6ade-4ecf-950f-fc78a552e655",
                                                "sense_id": "a8f64782-0ea9-3749-a3e6-b7032e69ae64",
                                                "text": "For example, in the Aaronide blessing, only two of the six verbs are formally jussives, yet all have the same volitional sense."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0ee23f8-a7bd-4ed8-89dc-9c1fc5335ca2",
                                                "sense_id": "a8f64782-0ea9-3749-a3e6-b7032e69ae64",
                                                "text": "As far as the jussive goes — ignoring the very few occurrences of this in first person — it can be noted that most of the second-person jussives are in negative commands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78901043-5593-49c3-b81c-79832ff29373",
                                                "sense_id": "a8f64782-0ea9-3749-a3e6-b7032e69ae64",
                                                "text": "If, on the other hand, reference is made purely to the root, we would expect all frequentative jussives to appear with a front element, producing *mɨt′ət′ɨs instead of mɨt′ət′ɨs (19d)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d36466a7-5486-48ca-b2bd-a8a2625d2c2c",
                                                "sense_id": "a8f64782-0ea9-3749-a3e6-b7032e69ae64",
                                                "text": "The jussive and cohortative usually convey more indirect, or more subtle, expressions of volition than the imperative does."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32ea1667-ad1e-3580-85cf-0d41d7f8ee27",
                                        "entry_id": "5ff18e31-b6c8-31b6-96ba-2fb37d7d11b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A verbal mood of vague or miscellaneous senses, occurring after some particles and in conditional clauses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Arabic",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
